TASK 7 — LVM: Build, Mount, and Extend Storage  (20 pts)
Zadatak 7 — LVM: izgradnja, montiranje i proširenje pohrane
Topic / Tema: parted, pvcreate, vgcreate, lvcreate, mkfs.xfs, fstab, lvextend, xfs_growfs
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A raw, empty disk is attached to your VM alongside the OS disk. Turn it into
a persistently-mounted LVM volume and then grow it.
Prazan, sirovi disk je priključen na vaš VM uz OS disk. Pretvorite ga u
trajno montirani LVM volumen i proširite ga.

IMPORTANT / VAŽNO: Do NOT hardcode /dev/sda or /dev/sdb in fstab. The kernel
can assign the disk letters in either order across reboots (both disks are on
the same SCSI bus). Always identify the empty disk first, then use the stable
LV path in fstab — not the device letter.
NEMOJTE tvrdo kodirati /dev/sda ili /dev/sdb u fstab. Jezgra može dodijeliti
slova diska u bilo kojim redoslijedu pri ponovnom pokretanju (oba diska su na
istoj SCSI sabirnici). Uvijek prvo identificirajte prazan disk, zatim
koristite stabilnu LV putanju u fstab — ne slovo uređaja.

Step 0 — Identify the empty disk (not the OS disk) / Korak 0 — Identificirajte prazan disk:
  lsblk            # find the disk with no partitions / nađite disk bez particija
  # The OS disk backs /. The other one is your LVM disk.
  # OS disk podupire /. Drugi je vaš LVM disk.

1. Partition the empty disk for LVM use (one partition, LVM flag set).
   Create a physical volume and a volume group named vg_practice.
   Particionirajte prazan disk za LVM (jedna particija, postavljena LVM oznaka).
   Stvorite fizički volumen i grupu volumena pod nazivom vg_practice.

2. Create a logical volume named lv_practice with an initial size of 300M
   in vg_practice. Format it XFS and mount it persistently at
   /storage/practice (must survive a reboot).
   Use the LV device path in fstab — /dev/vg_practice/lv_practice is stable
   across reboots (unlike raw sd* letters), so UUID is optional here.
   Stvorite logički volumen pod nazivom lv_practice početne veličine 300M
   u vg_practice. Formatirajte ga kao XFS i trajno montirajte na
   /storage/practice (mora preživjeti ponovno pokretanje).
   Koristite LV putanju u fstab — /dev/vg_practice/lv_practice je stabilna
   kroz ponovljeno pokretanje (za razliku od slova sd*), UUID nije obavezan.

3. Create the file /storage/practice/marker.txt with the exact content:
   Stvorite datoteku /storage/practice/marker.txt s točnim sadržajem:
     practice volume ready

4. Extend lv_practice by 500M and grow the XFS filesystem to use the new
   space — without unmounting or losing the marker file.
   Proširite lv_practice za 500M i povećajte XFS datotečni sustav da
   iskoristi novi prostor — bez odmontiranja ili gubitka marker datoteke.

5. Reboot once to verify the persistent mount / Jednom restartajte za provjeru:
     sudo systemctl reboot

Hint / Savjet:
      lsblk -fp shows filesystem type and mountpoint for each disk/partition.
      lsblk -fp prikazuje vrstu datotečnog sustava i točku montiranja.
      parted <disk> mklabel gpt
      parted <disk> mkpart primary 1MiB 100%
      parted <disk> set 1 lvm on
      pvcreate <disk>1  →  vgcreate vg_practice <disk>1
      lvcreate -L 300M -n lv_practice vg_practice
      mkfs.xfs /dev/vg_practice/lv_practice
      /dev/vg_practice/lv_practice is a stable path — safe to use in fstab.
      /dev/vg_practice/lv_practice je stabilna putanja — sigurno koristiti u fstab.
      After lvextend / Nakon lvextend: xfs_growfs /storage/practice


TASK 8 — Persistent Logging: journald + rsyslog  (15 pts)
Zadatak 8 — Trajno bilježenje: journald + rsyslog
Topic / Tema: systemd-journald, /etc/systemd/journald.conf, rsyslog, logger
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Configure two logging improvements.
Konfigurirajte dva poboljšanja u bilježenju.

1. Configure systemd-journald to store logs persistently on disk so they
   survive reboots. (The journal is currently volatile — in-memory only.)
   Konfigurirajte systemd-journald da trajno pohranjuje zapise na disk kako
   bi preživjeli ponovljeno pokretanje. (Journal je trenutno nestalan — samo u memoriji.)

2. Create an rsyslog configuration file under /etc/rsyslog.d/ that routes
   all messages matching facility local3 at priority warning (and above)
   to the file /var/log/practice-events.
   Stvorite rsyslog konfiguracijsku datoteku u /etc/rsyslog.d/ koja usmjerava
   sve poruke facility local3 na razini warning (i više) u datoteku
   /var/log/practice-events.

3. Generate a test log message with the correct facility and priority:
   Generirajte testnu poruku s ispravnom facility i priority:
     logger -p local3.warning "test message"
   Confirm it appears in /var/log/practice-events.
   Potvrdite da se pojavljuje u /var/log/practice-events.

4. Reboot to verify the persistent journal survives / Restartajte za provjeru:
     sudo systemctl reboot

Hint / Savjet: Persistent journald requires the directory /var/log/journal/ to
      exist before restarting systemd-journald (or editing Storage= in journald.conf).
      Trajna pohrana journald zahtijeva da direktorij /var/log/journal/ postoji
      prije ponovnog pokretanja systemd-journald (ili uređivanja Storage= u journald.conf).
      Rsyslog routing syntax / Sintaksa usmjeravanja:
        local3.warning    /var/log/practice-events
      Place config files in /etc/rsyslog.d/<name>.conf and restart rsyslog.
      Smjestite konfiguracijske datoteke u /etc/rsyslog.d/<naziv>.conf i
      restartajte rsyslog.


TASK 9 — SELinux: File Context and Boolean  (15 pts)
Zadatak 9 — SELinux: kontekst datoteke i boolean
Topic / Tema: getenforce, ls -Z, chcon, semanage fcontext, restorecon, setsebool, getsebool
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A web file has a wrong SELinux context and a required boolean is disabled.
Fix both problems persistently.
Web datoteka ima pogrešan SELinux kontekst i potrebni boolean je onemogućen.
Ispravite oba problema trajno.

Current state (set at provisioning) / Trenutno stanje (postavljeno pri inicijalizaciji):
  /var/www/html/practice.html has SELinux type var_t (wrong / pogrešno)
  httpd_can_network_connect_db boolean is off / boolean je isključen

1. Verify SELinux is in Enforcing mode. If it is not, set it back.
   (Do NOT set it to Permissive — that defeats the purpose.)
   Provjerite da je SELinux u Enforcing modu. Ako nije, vratite ga.
   (NEMOJTE ga postaviti na Permissive — to poništava svrhu.)

2. Fix the SELinux context on /var/www/html/practice.html so it has the
   type httpd_sys_content_t.
   The fix must be persistent — use semanage fcontext + restorecon,
   not just chcon (chcon alone does not survive restorecon or relabel).
   Ispravite SELinux kontekst na /var/www/html/practice.html da ima tip
   httpd_sys_content_t. Ispravak mora biti trajan — koristite
   semanage fcontext + restorecon, ne samo chcon (chcon ne preživljava
   restorecon ili relabel).

3. Enable the httpd_can_network_connect_db boolean persistently:
   Trajno omogućite httpd_can_network_connect_db boolean:
     sudo setsebool -P httpd_can_network_connect_db on

Hint / Savjet: Check current context / Provjerite trenutni kontekst:
        ls -Z /var/www/html/practice.html
      Fix with semanage / Ispravite semanage naredbom:
        sudo semanage fcontext -a -t httpd_sys_content_t '/var/www/html/practice\.html'
        sudo restorecon -v /var/www/html/practice.html
      List booleans / Popis booleana: getsebool -a | grep httpd


TASK 10 — Podman: Build, Run, and Persist a Container  (15 pts)
Zadatak 10 — Podman: izgradnja, pokretanje i trajnost kontejnera
Topic / Tema: Containerfile, podman build, podman run, podman generate systemd, systemctl --user
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The dev team needs a custom web container that keeps running after logout.
Razvojnom timu potreban je prilagođeni web kontejner koji ostaje aktivan
i nakon odjave.

1. Create the directory /home/student/webapp/ and inside it create a file
   named Containerfile with this content (replace BASE_IMAGE with the actual
   image name shown below):
   Stvorite direktorij /home/student/webapp/ i unutar njega datoteku
   Containerfile s ovim sadržajem (zamijenite BASE_IMAGE s nazivom slike
   prikazanim ispod):

     FROM {{ practice_base_image }}
     RUN echo "Practice web server" > /var/www/html/index.html

2. Build the image and tag it as practice-web:1.0:
   Izgradite sliku i označite je kao practice-web:1.0:
     podman build -t practice-web:1.0 /home/student/webapp/

3. Run the image as a detached container named practice-srv, mapping
   host port 8180 to the container's port 8080:
   Pokrenite sliku kao odvojeni kontejner pod nazivom practice-srv,
   mapiranjem porta 8180 na port kontejnera 8080:
     podman run -d --name practice-srv -p 8180:8080 practice-web:1.0
   Verify / Provjerite: curl localhost:8180   should return / treba vratiti
   "Practice web server"

4. Make the container persist across logout and reboot using a systemd unit:
   Učinite kontejner trajnim kroz odjavu i ponovljeno pokretanje
   koristeći systemd jedinicu:
     podman generate systemd --new --files --name practice-srv
     mkdir -p ~/.config/systemd/user
     mv container-practice-srv.service ~/.config/systemd/user/
     systemctl --user daemon-reload
     systemctl --user enable --now container-practice-srv
   Then reboot / Zatim restartajte: sudo systemctl reboot

Hint / Savjet: The base image is pre-pulled — no internet access needed.
      Osnovna slika je unaprijed preuzeta — nije potreban pristup internetu.
      "podman ps" shows running containers / prikazuje aktivne kontejnere.
      "systemctl --user status container-practice-srv" shows unit status.
      linger must be enabled for your user so units survive logout
      (loginctl enable-linger student — already done at provisioning).
      linger mora biti omogućen za vašeg korisnika da jedinice prežive odjavu
      (loginctl enable-linger student — već postavljeno pri inicijalizaciji).


